{"title":"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ratio of the measures of two acute angles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad0a4bc0ad5d6415575678e779682fb207069c5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5:4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />, and the complement of one of these two angles is twice as large as the complement of the other. What is the sum of the degree measures of the two angles?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/1/1413d92141324ac3232d118be4e1533d6d5befc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 75\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 90\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 135\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 150\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 270$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can set up a system of equations where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are the two acute angles. WLOG, assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262a080d0d87e973b817945967a512346d8bfc49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in order for the complement of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to be greater than the complement of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf35c47933e3a4ca4cc7cbe772c8eac6da774965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add22d9bda21e86390bc74fa4dde17730a442da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4a13b162a331ab567d4fcefe066a34f349e6bf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add22d9bda21e86390bc74fa4dde17730a442da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7e157113df4f31f54bbf87bd7c693edbd40f1d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in the first equation and substituting into the second equation yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/37605e261d79ab5f53fd1c8add55b71c9584dbfc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} 90 - x &amp; = 2 (90 - 1.25x) \\\\ 1.5x &amp; = 90 \\\\ x &amp; = 60 \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"63\" />\n</p><p>Substituting this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> value back into the first equation yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e4c2930d79c57bee209557767b878cd704ea46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cf26be132ef93923e082ee4153b2cb0ef44a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/414da89c5cbe83120d734b32f0077b98684aa15f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 135}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>(Solution by akaashp11)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We let the measures be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4977828049d99f20ccd3b4acb6bbd43c2eb70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> giving us the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad0a4bc0ad5d6415575678e779682fb207069c5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5:4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2ccbf1b7ca9297986577a7fa0f07e7642c1f7238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90-4x&gt;90-5x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" /> since this inequality gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e28efa00c4f2c66d1aa381c0cb1f8e0ef8d6e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, which is true since the measures of angles are never negative. We also know the bigger complement is twice the smaller, so \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eb41acdd9e544c6f63ace29b8d7c893472aaa73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90-4x=2(90-5x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc06c69f0969acde4ca9f84cf38b1a287b932ac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90-4x=180-10x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"161\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0eed227a6427a636a4d7a1e07de82d87fc7a3ff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x=90$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e45a63c78330a7020ad39fd035c818528f54ff46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the angles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7e4c2930d79c57bee209557767b878cd704ea46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/414da89c5cbe83120d734b32f0077b98684aa15f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 135}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4LsOG_HPYn8\">https://youtu.be/4LsOG_HPYn8</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/x1rKDLjWNjg\">https://youtu.be/x1rKDLjWNjg</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B\">2016 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\